<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="SweetGeorgieFame-C-Theme" spTempo="120">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1966
Composer:	Blossom Dearie
Lyricist:	Sandra Black Harris
Form:	64-bar AABA
Style:	Jazz Waltz Medium
Key:	C Major

Blossom Dearie wrote the tune in London in 1966 after hearing
Georgie Fame perform and seeing children dance to his records;
Sandra Black Harris supplied the lyrics. Dearie first performed it
publicly at Ronnie Scott’s in 1967, and later recorded it herself;
some credits shorten the lyricist’s name to Sandra Harris. </spComments>
